From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onyx contributors <onyx@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:11:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] WIP: PORT=Onyx for WTF, bmalloc and JavaScriptCore
 (step 1 of the Onyx port)

What: a new port, Onyx (a small OS for the Raspberry Pi 4, AArch64; static programs, 64 KB pages,
newlib + libonyxposix, no GLib, no executable memory): Source/cmake/OptionsOnyx.cmake (static
libraries, no JIT, C_LOOP by default, no WebAssembly / sampling profiler / remote inspector,
system malloc, 64 KB page block), Onyx in WebKitCommon.cmake's ports and OS detection (WTF_OS_ONYX),
OS(ONYX) in PlatformOS.h (a Unix), CeilingOnPageSize 64 KB, WTF/wtf/PlatformOnyx.cmake (POSIX and
Unix sources, the generic run loop / work queue / main thread), wtf/onyx/ memory status over
getrusage, bmalloc/PlatformOnyx.cmake (no libpas with the system malloc),
JavaScriptCore/PlatformOnyx.cmake.
Why: build the jsc shell for Onyx; the port model is PlayStation / JSCOnly / Haiku.
Status: configures; bmalloc builds; WTF stops at wtf/PlatformRegisters.h (sys/ucontext.h).
